00:40:06.000 --> 00:40:13.040 align:start position:19%
amending 5.7.3
accessory dwelling units of the Cheyenne

00:40:11.280 --> 00:40:18.480 align:start position:19%
Unified Development Code. To remove
owner occupancy and adjust parking

00:40:15.440 --> 00:40:24.160 align:start position:19%
requirements for accessory dwellings and
making conforming amendments to the

00:40:20.400 --> 00:40:29.520 align:start position:19%
definitions of an accessory dwelling and
semi-attached dwelling under 1.4.4, 4

00:40:27.520 --> 00:40:32.520 align:start position:19%
descriptions of uses of land and
buildings.

00:40:34.560 --> 00:40:39.040 align:start position:19%
&gt;&gt; Mr. Lloyd, staff report, please.
&gt;&gt; Mr. Chair, members of the committee, my

00:40:37.680 --> 00:40:41.760 align:start position:19%
name is Seth Lloyd. I'm with the City of
Shine Planning and Development

00:40:40.000 --> 00:40:44.720 align:start position:19%
Department. The proposal in front of you
makes amendments to the Unified

00:40:43.040 --> 00:40:48.960 align:start position:19%
Development Codes standards for
accessory dwelling units. Essentially,

00:40:46.640 --> 00:40:54.079 align:start position:19%
it removes one requirement and changes
another one. The removal is for owner

00:40:51.359 --> 00:40:58.960 align:start position:19%
occupancy and the change is to um the
parking requirements. Essentially, the

00:40:56.400 --> 00:41:03.359 align:start position:19%
parking requirement change um
redefineses uh the extra space as being

00:41:01.280 --> 00:41:07.200 align:start position:19%
anywhere um on the property as opposed
to being in a discrete portion of the

00:41:04.720 --> 00:41:11.839 align:start position:19%
lot, allowing us to use um say a
threecar driveway or three um or on

00:41:10.400 --> 00:41:15.680 align:start position:19%
street parking in the case of a corner
lot, whatever it needs to be to allow a

00:41:13.920 --> 00:41:20.480 align:start position:19%
little more flexibility on the parking.
For the owner occupancy side of things,

00:41:18.160 --> 00:41:24.000 align:start position:19%
um the current code requires owner
occupancy of an accessory dwelling unit.

00:41:22.240 --> 00:41:28.240 align:start position:19%
So, if you have a single family home,
you can convert it to two units if you

00:41:26.079 --> 00:41:32.880 align:start position:19%
are living in one of those two units.
Um, or you can add a garage on the back

00:41:30.640 --> 00:41:38.160 align:start position:19%
with a dwelling unit above the garage.
Those are some options for an accessory

00:41:34.480 --> 00:41:41.680 align:start position:19%
dwelling unit. Um, in under our current
unified development code, a flat over

00:41:39.680 --> 00:41:45.280 align:start position:19%
flat duplex is considered a duplex. And
so, if you have enough street frontage

00:41:43.280 --> 00:41:48.319 align:start position:19%
on your property, you can still do two
units even if you're going to rent out

00:41:46.560 --> 00:41:52.000 align:start position:19%
both units and not live there. You just
have to have a certain minimum amount of

00:41:49.760 --> 00:41:56.240 align:start position:19%
frontage. Um, in the unified development
code, for example, um, one of our lot

00:41:53.920 --> 00:42:01.839 align:start position:19%
types requires a 30 feet of lot frontage
for a duplex. Um, so if you had a single

00:41:59.280 --> 00:42:05.680 align:start position:19%
family home with 65 ft of lot frontage,
you could do two units as a flat over

00:42:03.680 --> 00:42:09.920 align:start position:19%
flat duplex as opposed to as an
accessory dwelling unit. This does

00:42:08.079 --> 00:42:13.920 align:start position:19%
trigger some changes in our building
code um, between the duplex and

00:42:11.760 --> 00:42:17.280 align:start position:19%
accessory dwelling unit. um our building
official has in the past treated an

00:42:15.839 --> 00:42:20.480 align:start position:19%
accessory dwelling unit as basically
extra rooms on a single family home

00:42:18.960 --> 00:42:24.000 align:start position:19%
because the owner is living there.
Whereas if it's going to be two rental

00:42:21.920 --> 00:42:29.119 align:start position:19%
units or a duplex or a flat or flat
duplex, it has to meet a higher standard

00:42:25.839 --> 00:42:35.839 align:start position:19%
in the building code. Um so by changing
accessory dwelling units to being

00:42:31.119 --> 00:42:40.000 align:start position:19%
allowed without um a uh owner being
occupied, the building code would look

00:42:37.839 --> 00:42:43.119 align:start position:19%
at an accessory dwelling the exact same
way as they would look at a flat

00:42:41.119 --> 00:42:45.680 align:start position:19%
overflat duplex. So, they would have
whether it's an accessory dwelling unit

00:42:44.240 --> 00:42:49.760 align:start position:19%
or duplex, whatever you call it, it
would have to meet those fire and

00:42:46.800 --> 00:42:54.560 align:start position:19%
building code standards. Um, in other
jurisdictions that have adopted uh ADUs

00:42:52.800 --> 00:42:57.200 align:start position:19%
without owner occupancy requirements,
this is how the building officials all

00:42:55.839 --> 00:43:00.079 align:start position:19%
look at them. It doesn't really matter
if it's a duplex or an accessory

00:42:58.400 --> 00:43:03.520 align:start position:19%
dwelling unit, they always have to meet
building and fire code as if it was a

00:43:01.599 --> 00:43:07.280 align:start position:19%
duplex. There's not really a it's more
of a zoning semantics than it is a a

00:43:05.440 --> 00:43:11.760 align:start position:19%
building code semantics for those other
jurisdictions. Um so that would change a

00:43:10.000 --> 00:43:18.880 align:start position:19%
little bit as far as construction of
materials go um for converting a house

00:43:14.480 --> 00:43:22.640 align:start position:19%
to two units. Um as such um because the
differentiation between a flat or flat

00:43:20.319 --> 00:43:27.520 align:start position:19%
duplex and ADU is basically lost. This
amendment also changes the definition

00:43:25.200 --> 00:43:30.640 align:start position:19%
section of uh uses in the unified
development code to clarify that a flat

00:43:28.960 --> 00:43:35.200 align:start position:19%
or flat duplex is always an accessory
dwelling unit. Um that also removes some

00:43:33.359 --> 00:43:40.000 align:start position:19%
of the challenges staff had with using
the SD lot types in the unified

00:43:37.040 --> 00:43:43.440 align:start position:19%
development code for duplexes because um
clearly when you look at the diagrams of

00:43:41.920 --> 00:43:46.079 align:start position:19%
the SD lot types in the unified
development code, they consider

00:43:44.400 --> 00:43:50.400 align:start position:19%
sidebyside duplexes. They don't really
consider the flat or flat version. And

00:43:48.319 --> 00:43:54.319 align:start position:19%
so it was a little bit wonky to try and
apply um the standards of the SD lot

00:43:52.240 --> 00:43:59.359 align:start position:19%
type to a flat overflat duplex. Um we
did our best we but by making this

00:43:57.359 --> 00:44:05.680 align:start position:19%
change um that change would happen to
that section of code as well.

00:44:01.280 --> 00:44:08.400 align:start position:19%
Um the uh I would note that there's been
um I mean obviously there's other

00:44:07.359 --> 00:44:13.040 align:start position:19%
jurisdictions that have made this
amendment. The state of Montana as a

00:44:10.000 --> 00:44:16.240 align:start position:19%
whole has made this amendment. Um and
there are various housing groups that

00:44:14.480 --> 00:44:22.079 align:start position:19%
feel like this is a a good path forward
for addressing some housing concerns. Um

00:44:19.599 --> 00:44:25.520 align:start position:19%
and as I noted previously, some lots can
do this anyway if they just have enough

00:44:23.760 --> 00:44:28.079 align:start position:19%
frontage. They could rent out both units
if they just have enough frontage

00:44:26.720 --> 00:44:35.040 align:start position:19%
because it becomes a flat or flat
duplex. So that is the impetus behind

00:44:30.480 --> 00:44:39.040 align:start position:19%
this. Um I would also note that our uh
various agencies have written letters of

00:44:37.200 --> 00:44:43.680 align:start position:19%
